cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or scoring suite, please cite as follows. Components carry different licenses — consonantal text: public domain; annotation data (Tiers 2-4): CC0-1.0; scholarly framework and compilation: CC-BY-4.0. See LICENSE.md for the authoritative statement."
type: dataset
title: "Open Masorah Masoretic Benchmark: a 4-tier CER evaluation suite for medieval Tiberian Hebrew (pilot benchmark, Leningrad Codex Deuteronomy)"
abstract: "A pilot four-tier inter-annotator-agreement benchmark and Character Error Rate scorer for medieval Tiberian Hebrew manuscript transcription. Scope: 96 verses across four folio sides of a single manuscript (Leningrad Codex, Deuteronomy 31:28-34:12), transcribed independently by two annotators and adjudicated to consensus. Tiers score consonants, nikkud, full text, and tier-4 meta-marks (circellus, rafe). Inter-annotator agreement, measured between the two blind pre-adjudication transcriptions, is CER 0.0029 / 0.0031 / 0.0130 at tiers 1-3 and detection F1 0.9187 at tier 4."
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-04"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - CC0-1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Lamm
    given-names: Ben
  - family-names: Ginsberg
    given-names: Yosef
  - family-names: Moster
    given-names: David Zev
  - family-names: Finkelstein
    given-names: Ari
repository-code: "https://github.com/openmasorah/masoretic-benchmark"
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/openmasorah/masoretic-benchmark-v0.1"
    description: "Hugging Face dataset distribution"
keywords:
  - hebrew
  - tiberian
  - manuscript
  - masoretic
  - leningrad-codex
  - ocr
  - htr
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - character-error-rate
  - nikkud
  - trop
  - digital-humanities
references:
  # --- Data sources ---
  - type: data
    title: "Unicode/XML Leningrad Codex: UXLC 2.5 (27.6)"
    authors:
      - name: "Tanach.us Inc."
    year: 2026
    url: "https://tanach.us/"
    notes: >-
      Tier-1 ground truth (folios F119A/F119B/F120A) and the UXLC backbone for
      tier-2 scoring are derived from UXLC. The biblical Hebrew text is free to
      view or copy without restriction; citation to Tanach.us is appreciated.
      License: https://tanach.us/License.html
  - type: historical-work
    title: "Leningrad Codex (Codex Leningradensis), Firkovich MS Evr. I B19a"
    authors:
      - name: "Samuel ben Jacob (scribe)"
    year: 1008
    url: "https://archive.org/details/Leningrad_Codex_Color_Images"
    notes: >-
      Base manuscript. National Library of Russia, St. Petersburg. Photographs by
      the West Semitic Research Project (Bruce E. Zuckerman et al.), which asserts
      rights over them. Manuscript images are referenced via IIIF only and never
      redistributed. (The Internet Archive item Leningrad_Codex_Color_Images
      carries a Public Domain Mark applied by an uploader, not by WSRP.)
